{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChPqvbyuKF1FXnD2e4GyS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've addressed the review findings on #386. I added the missing \"waiting for inputs\" status count and the tests the plan named. The targeted `go test` runs pass, but `make lint test` timed out here, so the full suite hasn't run. I didn't write `TestCloserHasNetwork` for `servecmd`.\n\n**Status issue.** The gate now records one `wait` gate event when it starts waiting for inputs and one `inputs-ready` event when they land. The daily digest shows a \"Waiting for inputs\" count of open issues whose newest gate event is the wait. The line is left out when the count is zero. To read those events the gate needed `Events` on the triage `Store` interface.\n\n**Tests added.**\n- **`internal/closeout/round_test.go` (new):**\n  - persisted round state;\n  - an unclosed worker record still opening a round;\n  - no second re-arm on a human re-request;\n  - Resume replaying the stored plan after the store changes;\n  - inputs redaction and the `inputsLost` needs-human path;\n  - `InputsOf` and `NetworkRoundCount`.\n- **`internal/triage` tests (inputs, intake, harness, loop):**\n  - approval markers per round and a stale approval being ignored;\n  - an approval given while inputs are missing counting once they land;\n  - the lead re-armed before the gate;\n  - main read errors leaving the issue waiting;\n  - symlink and submodule entries counting as missing;\n  - one main read per tick, with the cache dropped on a new SHA;\n  - the wait and ready events;\n  - the re-armed lead being re-claimed.\n- **`internal/digest` test:** the new waiting count.\n\n**Docs.** `docs/proposal.md` now has the label state machine and status-issue notes. The re-arm, persisted state, `Clear`, gate and approval were already described there.\n\n**Testing.**\n- `go vet` and `go test` pass for `closeout`, `triage`, `digest`, `servecmd`, `roles`, `docscheck` and `state`.\n- `make lint test` as a whole timed out after 2 minutes.\n- `go vet ./...` fails on a parse error in `internal/roles/testdata/docs/skips/src/_x.go`, which is not part of this change.\n\n**Not done.** I skipped `TestCloserHasNetwork`. The closer doesn't expose its deps, and a behavioural test would need a full git worktree. The wiring is one line in `reaping.go`.\n\nThe report is in `.ard/386/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1297,"cache_read_input_tokens":105351,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1297},"output_tokens":737,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2f1a6b2e-e8cb-4137-ab71-597118ce4930","uuid":"e959674b-7b8e-4283-83bc-cc74c463b96b","timestamp":"2026-11-25T14:59:04.617Z","request_id":"req_011ChPqvbpyMtGKHCKZJaHvB"}
